From ca0b5bd732b98516b701d264e6831a5799aa355f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 09:15:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] SD file access over USB MIDI (SysEx JSON protocol from 1.3)

Port of community firmware 1.3's smSysex file access, so that browser
apps like DEx (file browser) and deluge-editor can list, read, write,
rename, copy, move and delete files on the SD card over USB.

- storage/smsysex.{h,cpp}: 1.3 protocol handler (session, ping, dir,
  open, close, read, write, delete, mkdir, rename, copy, move, utime).
  1.2.1 changes: reply buffer allocated on first use, requests from DIN
  ignored (no overflow protection there), oversized requests dropped,
  queue bounded at 16. A reply goes out only as a whole, once the USB
  send buffer has room for all of it, and is dropped after two seconds
  without room instead of being sent in part. A directory page takes an
  entry back out if it would make the reply too big for that buffer.
  A write without a decode buffer reports FR_NOT_ENOUGH_CORE.
- io/midi: the USB MIDI send ring holds 4096 messages instead of 1024
  (in the internal frunk RAM, which has room), so a full directory page
  of 25 entries fits even with 255-character names. deluge-editor ends
  a listing at the first page shorter than 25 entries. A full ring now
  drops the new message instead of overwriting the oldest unsent one.
- storage/smsysex_json.{h,cpp}: the memory-based JSON writer/reader
  from 1.3, which the protocol needs. Names with bytes outside ASCII are
  escaped as \u00XX, so replies stay clean 7-bit SysEx.
- util/pack.c: unpack_7bit_to_8bit returns the decoded length, as in
  1.3 (1.2.1 returned the encoded length, which no caller used).
- io/midi: SysEx command 0x04 (Json) goes to smSysex; 0x05 is JsonReply.
- deluge.cpp: repeating task that works through queued requests.
- fatfs: FF_USE_CHMOD on, for f_utime (keeps file dates on upload).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Eb214cM1zi1k5Gpcn9RLKh
